import{at as e,it as t,n,vt as r}from"./chunks/framework.fhiXEbOi.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Integrate Pay-to-Play payments","description":"Bind a service to the correct payment contract, reserve invoice authorizations, sign v2 vouchers and reconcile actual collection.","frontmatter":{"title":"Integrate Pay-to-Play payments","description":"Bind a service to the correct payment contract, reserve invoice authorizations, sign v2 vouchers and reconcile actual collection.","outline":false},"headers":[],"relativePath":"pay-to-play/integration.md","filePath":"pay-to-play/integration.md"}`),a={name:`pay-to-play/integration.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return r(),t(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[e(`<h1 id="integrate-invoice-authorized-payments" tabindex="-1">Integrate invoice-authorized payments <a class="header-anchor" href="#integrate-invoice-authorized-payments" aria-label="Permalink to “Integrate invoice-authorized payments”">​</a></h1><div class="ported-guide"><p>The contract settles cumulative authority; your service owns purchase identity, acceptance, allocation and delivery. Begin with <a href="./">the balance and voucher model</a>. This guide follows source <code>04a18763</code>, not every historical deployment.</p><nav aria-label="Guide sections"><a href="#binding">Identify</a> · <a href="#reserve">Reserve</a> · <a href="#sign">Sign</a> · <a href="#collect">Collect</a> · <a href="#compatibility">Migrate</a></nav><h2 id="binding">1. Identify the actual payment contract</h2><p>Read <code>camManifest()</code> and <code>contractAddress(&quot;PayToPlay&quot;)</code> from the trusted CAM host. Check the selected chain, exact resource bytes and bound payment address. The EIP-712 verifying contract is <strong>PayToPlay, not the CAM host</strong>.</p><p>Compare that address with the signing projection&#39;s domain and the transaction-review target. Reload an open viewer after publication/binding changes; a read refresh alone can retain cached resources. The projection rejects a host whose payment binding differs from its immutable backing, but that does not prove every cached viewer address agrees. Adding a projection moves no funds and revokes no voucher.</p><h2 id="reserve">2. Reserve one durable authorization interval</h2><p>Serialize reservations per <code>(chain, paymentContract, customer, channelId)</code>. Persist the purchase ID and its interval before a retry can create another increase. Use the previous authorized total, not merely the latest on-chain paid total. Two concurrent purchases cannot both reserve the same interval and then count as independent revenue.</p><p>Agree on an invoice codec before signing. The supplied <a href="https://github.com/numpde/dapp32/blob/04a18763700bbaa25cad73b9806d236ab4d5e139/js/tools/pay-to-play-vouchers/README.md">invoice/voucher helper reference</a> owns its normalized <code>PayToPlayInvoice/1</code> encoding, SHA-256 preimage, fixed vector and acceptance API. Its separately documented peer exact-byte vector is a different codec. Do not hash arbitrary pretty-printed JSON or substitute one codec&#39;s hash for the other.</p><p>Keep immutable invoice/terms documents separate from mutable acceptance, fulfillment, cancellation and refund records. The helper validates structure and caller-supplied context; it does not authenticate an invoice issuer, reserve backing, lock a database row or deliver a service.</p><h2 id="sign">3. Sign with the confirmed permanent key</h2><p>Read the position&#39;s confirmed nonzero <code>voucherKey</code>. That key signs; <code>customer</code> remains the balance owner even when the addresses differ.</p><div class="language-text" dir="ltr"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">text</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark" style="--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>Domain:</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  name: &quot;PayToPlay&quot;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  version: &quot;2&quot;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  chainId: the deployment chain</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  verifyingContract: the bound PayToPlay address</span></span>
<span class="line"><span></span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Voucher(address customer,uint256 channelId,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>        uint256 cumulativeTotal,bytes32 invoiceHash)</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Use canonical 65-byte <code>r,s,v</code> ECDSA with low s and v equal to 27 or 28. Compare the typed-data digest with <code>voucherDigest(customer, channelId, cumulativeTotal, invoiceHash)</code>. Do not personal-message-sign that digest or substitute the owner&#39;s current ERC-1271 approval. The signing-details screen supplies comparison data, not a signature or commercial acceptance.</p><p>Preserve every disclosed signature as potential exposure, including signatures attached to rejected or expired invoices. Acceptance expiry, cancellation, failed delivery and a commercial refund do <strong>not</strong> revoke the voucher or rewind its cumulative stream. A refunded open position can later be funded again; its old unpaid authority remains relevant.</p><h2 id="backing">4. Decide whether to accept work</h2><p>Verify the signature and confirmed key, then check current balance, pending ordinary withdrawal, outstanding authorizations/reservations and recovery cutoff. With balance B, request R, paid total P and greatest outstanding signed/reserved total A, one conservative admission policy for new work x is:</p><pre><code>max(A - P, 0) + x &lt;= max(B - R, 0)</code></pre><p>This is service policy, not an on-chain reservation. Collection can consume funds under a withdrawal request and race another collection or withdrawal. Stop new work when settling and allow time for inclusion, confirmations and transfer failure before the cutoff.</p><p>The updated source <a href="./#withdrawals">restarts the ordinary wait after a positive credit</a> when a request is pending. That changes <code>readyAt</code>, not admissible backing: if B = R = 100, the right-hand side remains zero even immediately after replenishment. A later invoice or voucher does not restart this clock. Work accepted near readiness can still lose to withdrawal; check the deployed runtime version and enforce confirmation, inclusion and delivery timing separately. Zero-period channels provide no positive exit window.</p><h2 id="collect">5. Collect, then allocate the observed payment</h2><pre><code>collect(customer, channelId, cumulativeTotal,
        invoiceHash, maxAmount, signature)</code></pre><p>Only the configured nonzero collector may submit. The admin can change that address or set zero to pause collection. <code>maxAmount</code> caps this call; it is not signed and does not prevent later partial collection. Payment goes to the channel&#39;s current payee, which the admin can change within the contract&#39;s rules.</p><p>Example: invoice A reserves 0→30 and B reserves 30→70. With nothing paid and balance 50, B&#39;s voucher can collect 50 and emit B&#39;s hash. Allocating in authorization order pays 30 toward A and 20 toward B—not 50 for B alone. Another 20 of backing permits the remainder. Different hashes at total 70 do not create more than 70 of cumulative authority.</p><p><code>VoucherCollected(customer, channelId, payee, amount, voucherPaid, invoiceHash)</code> records actual settlement, not invoice allocation. Customer, channel and payee are indexed; the hash is not. A valid zero collection emits no collection event, so a successful receipt alone proves no payment. Reconcile transaction/log identity and your reorganization policy, retaining earlier invoices separately.</p><h2 id="api">Use the deployed ABI and authored route</h2><p>Use the <a href="https://github.com/numpde/dapp32/blob/04a18763700bbaa25cad73b9806d236ab4d5e139/dapps/pay-to-play/cam/abi/PayToPlay.json">exact ABI</a> and <a href="https://github.com/numpde/dapp32/blob/04a18763700bbaa25cad73b9806d236ab4d5e139/dapps/pay-to-play/cam/main.json">route arguments</a>. Quantities/IDs are uint256, periods uint64 seconds, invoice references bytes32 and signatures bytes. The immutable <code>asset()</code> is the native-asset sentinel <code>0xEeeeeEeeeEeEeeEeEeEeeEEEeeeeEeeeeeeeEEeE</code>; it supplies no display symbol or decimals and does not enable ERC-20 deposits.</p><p>CAM continuation inputs are not necessarily Solidity arguments: <code>closeChannel</code> carries a customer for the next read; <code>move</code> maps its channel to the source; <code>fund</code> uses the amount as both argument and native value. Recovery events complement payment events, but time-only phase changes emit nothing. Monitor deadlines as well as logs.</p><h2 id="compatibility">Replace deployments explicitly</h2><p>Changing a manifest does not upgrade an older contract, tuple layout or selector. Use matching v2 resources and update signers, event consumers and refund-worker runtime-code pins together. New addresses have independent balances and permanent keys; old authorizations remain with the original deployment. No automatic voucher, key or balance migration exists.</p><p>Exercise the integration with the <a href="../development/payment-fixture.html">isolated fixture handoff</a> and <a href="../development/app-checks.html">app checks</a>. Contract authority: <a href="https://github.com/numpde/dapp32/blob/04a18763700bbaa25cad73b9806d236ab4d5e139/dapps/pay-to-play/src/PayToPlay.sol">PayToPlay.sol</a>.</p></div>`,2)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};